        ":question/id": "ea57ab4e-12f4-561c-891e-5ea3d2562a52",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6(x+1)\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(x+1)\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x+1)\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={(x+1)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={(x+1)}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({(x+1)}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$\n\nUse the real cube root during separation, on intervals where $y\\ne 0.$",
